# Vietnamese Translation Style

Canonical terminology: `docs/BẢNG QUY TẮC Chat GPT tongHop.md`

## Output shape

- Plain text only; **mirror source line-for-line**
- No consecutive duplicate empty lines — blank-line runs must match source
- No Markdown headings or editorial subsections in output
- Skill: `.cursor/skills/translate-buddhist-text/SKILL.md`

## Register

- Modern scholarly Vietnamese; neutral, objective; context-driven (not literal per character)
- Scripture (經): dignified, concise; preserve parallelism
- Commentary (疏/註): clearer syntax OK; keep glossary `vi` terms
- Prefer established Hán Việt in `vi`; thuần Việt gloss only when popularizing

## Capitalization (§14)

**Capitalize:** Phật, Như Lai, Thế Tôn, Bồ tát, A la hán, Đại Bồ tát, Tam Bảo, Chính pháp

**Lowercase (common nouns):** chúng sinh, phiền não, nghiệp, trí tuệ, công đức

Follow glossary for compounds (e.g. `Bát nhã ba la mật`, `ba la mật`).

## Forbidden synonyms

- 菩薩: never `Giác hữu tình`
- Monastic ranks: `Tỳ kheo`, `Sa di`, `Ưu bà tắc` — not `nam cư sĩ` / `nữ cư sĩ` (footnotes only)
- Sutra titles: `Kim Cương Kinh` pattern, not `Kinh Kim Cương`

## Dialogue

- Keep `「…」` nesting; do not add **Hỏi:** / **Đáp:** labels unless the source has 問/答 markers
- **Buddha → addressee:** when Phật / Như Lai / Thế Tôn / 婆伽婆 / 世尊 speaks **directly to** someone and the utterance opens with a vocative (大王, 善男子, …), prefix **`Này`** before the title or name — e.g. 「大王！…」→ 「Này Đại vương!…」
- Apply inside quoted speech only; not when a bodhisattva, disciple, or narrator speaks; not when there is no vocative in source
- Do not add a second `Này` if one is already present

## Grammar

- Prefer subject-verb-object; avoid excessive passive unless source requires
- Honorifics: 佛 → Phật; 世尊 → Thế Tôn
- Glossary-bound terms: use `vi` column only — never `hv` when they differ

## First occurrence

- Optional inline: `Bát nhã (般若)` for hard terms when user requests
- Otherwise use footnotes via web editor (`docs/style-guide.md` §5)
- Agents do not add annotations by default

## Numbers and Names

- Follow glossary `vi` and series convention
- Place names: Title Case per syllable, no hyphens (e.g. 文殊 → Văn Thù)

## Punctuation

- Vietnamese punctuation; no full-width Chinese punctuation
- Quotation of Dharma phrases: use « » or " " consistently within a series
- Spelling: one consistent variant per series (e.g. hy sinh, lý luận — no alternation)

See `docs/style-guide.md` for extended examples.
